.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T22:36:19-08:00","id":429849,"title":"","content":"Having just gone through the corebook, yes. We definitely need a book for each Tribe as Acrozatarim described them.<br /> <br /> I think it'd be better to have a separate book for Bale Hounds, all things considered; Kinslayers and Shadow Hunters would be great places to put them, but I get the sense that their popularity makes them need their own book. (Also, a separate book means I don't have to buy it.) Tribeless Ghost Wolves for a book is an interesting idea, but I'd rather frame it as an update to Blood of the Wolf, perhaps including formal rules for things like a Lodge becoming a full Tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T23:24:24-08:00","id":429919,"title":"","content":"I'm on board for this vision of the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-05T23:29:56-08:00","id":429924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=429849#post429849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having just gone through the corebook, yes. We definitely need a book for each Tribe as Acrozatarim described them.<br /> <br /> I think it'd be better to have a separate book for Bale Hounds, all things considered; Kinslayers and Shadow Hunters would be great places to put them, but I get the sense that their popularity makes them need their own book. (Also, a separate book means I don't have to buy it.) Tribeless Ghost Wolves for a book is an interesting idea, but I'd rather frame it as an update to Blood of the Wolf, perhaps including formal rules for things like a Lodge becoming a full Tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A possibility that crossed my mind was if Inferno got a 2Edition update, it could relevant chapters for different lines... not necessarily EVERY line, but the discussion of the Maeljin as the Werewolf view of what others call Archdemons, and the Bale Hounds as their pact-forming minions, would fit there. Could put Belial's Brood in the same book (bringing literal demons into the picture is a bit new for them, but with intentionally sinning to bargain for powers, it fits - I'm NOT saying do away with their ideology that they are enfleshed demons trying to achieve realization as what they truly are); a new Left-Handed Legacy for dealing with the Inferno; etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-06T06:23:25-08:00","id":430171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=429849#post429849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having just gone through the corebook, yes. We definitely need a book for each Tribe as Acrozatarim described them.<br /> <br /> I think it'd be better to have a separate book for Bale Hounds, all things considered; Kinslayers and Shadow Hunters would be great places to put them, but I get the sense that their popularity makes them need their own book. (Also, a separate book means I don't have to buy it.) Tribeless Ghost Wolves for a book is an interesting idea, but I'd rather frame it as an update to Blood of the Wolf, perhaps including formal rules for things like a Lodge becoming a full Tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a Bale Hounds lover ( I run a chronicle based on them, is not this obvious <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) I would want full book, seeing how only a chapter in <b>Blasphemies</b> still left me unsatisfied ( too short <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) - and Wounds itself <i>really</i> need more extrapolation in the game line. Still, I think that adding basic stuff about them to the Blood Talons book is very appropriate, as they are not in the corebook - Pure at least got those few pages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/memb