13"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T12:11:52-08:00","id":431612,"title":"","content":"I think a supplement to flesh out the Tribes should be the first supplement for Werewolf 2.0. I think the core book places a little too much emphasis on the chosen preys, and not on the broader cultures they might have. In 1e, I liked how the Hunters-in-Darkness were naturalists who dressed like hippies with a violent streak, how those who joined the Bone Shadows often had supernatural encounters before they Changed. The tribal section in 2e made me wonder: &quot;But what if I can't think of a reason why my character should consider that prey to be the most worthy or dangerous?&quot; I saw that each Tribe has a list of archetypes of people that would fit in there, and I'd like Onyx Path to expound upon that.<br /> <br /> A Tribes supplement could also provide a new list of Merits and/or pack tactics that give PCs new tricks to use against their tribe's chosen prey, thereby expounding upon that aspect as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-07T12:30:14-08:00","id":431633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=431080#post431080\" rel=\"nofollow\" ti