ent":"I think this thread is VERY relevant to Monday's Blogpost asking for pitches. I'm very much a fan of each Tribe getting its own book and think its a major disservice to have them shoved into just a single chapter like what we have in Tribes of the Moon. Lets get this idea in there instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T07:35:25-07:00","id":864283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=864274#post864274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this thread is VERY relevant to Monday's Blogpost asking for pitches. I'm very much a fan of each Tribe getting its own book and think its a major disservice to have them shoved into just a single chapter like what we have in Tribes of the Moon. Lets get this idea in there instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Already pitched it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T08:59:07-07:00","id":864326,"title":"","content":"The more people who indicate that it's the sort of thing they want to see, the more likely there's a chance of it being considered <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bEdit: Including people who indicated their support after Sikla Alkis stopped updating the OP, it's up to 52 supporters in this thread now. However, note that that number doesn't count for much if the people who make the decisions at OP don't become aware of it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","user":"Acrozatarim","date":". 04-12-2016, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T09:37:43-07:00","id":864349,"title":"","content":"I just linked to it and only then did I see you copypasted the whole thing already. XD<br /> <br /> Oh well, I'm pretty sure more people need to see these great ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T09:56:37-07:00","id":864361,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of good here. I just don't know if the tribes are so developed to warrant a whole book to them like the tribes from apocalypse... But then there's always new material to be written!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T10:15:19-07:00","id":864376,"title":"","content":"Don't know about Apocalypse, but considering we're talking about groups of shapeshifting demigods that have been around for thousands of years tied to Celestial Beings beyond mortal understanding I'd say we have quite a bit of history and customs we could dive into. Hell, how they view their Sacred Prey alone should be world a chapter.<br /> <br /> That we've gone through two editions and people still think they can easily be swapped out says quite a bit about their needed to be developed more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T10:22:18-07:00","id":864383,"title":"","content":"Yes. If they're confined to three pages in the front of the core book they won't really be developed beyond that. The tribes of Apocalypse wouldn't have any depth if they were still confined to the few pages in the core book.<br /> <br /> Though Tribes of the Moon went a nice distance in fleshing them out, it's really something they could use their own books for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-12-2016, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T10:32:28-07:00","id":864385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=864376#post864376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't know about Apocalypse, but considering we're talking about groups of shapeshifting demigods that have been around for thousands of years tied to Celestial Beings beyond mortal understanding I'd say we have quite a bit of history and customs we could dive into. Hell, how they view their Sacred Prey alone should be world a chapter.<br /> <br /> That we've gone through two editions and people still think they can easily be swapped out says quite a bit about their needed to be developed more.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that Tribes in Forsaken don't come with cultural or ethnic baggage like they do in Apocalypse (Tribes are used more literally as a collection of bloodlines and relatives: you're born into a Tribe rather than choosing which Tribe you join). So you might list examples of what a Forsaken Tribe looks like in a given area. The Blood Talons of the Hippo Valley in Zimbabwe will look quite different from the Blood Talons in Alice Springs, Australia. You'd cover those cultural identifiers in Hunting Ground entries about those Tribes though, not in a big book. However, you could put the few cultural identifiers that they <i>do</i> share in a single chapter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T10:58:09-07:00","id":864395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=864361#post864361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a lot of good here. I just don't know if the tribes are so developed to warrant a whole book to them like the tribes from apocalypse... But then there's always new material to be written!</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you read the pitches? They're huge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:25:17-07:00","id":864431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=864361#post864361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a lot of good here. I just don't know if the tribes are so developed to warrant a whole book to them like the tribes from apocalypse... But then there's always new material to be written!</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason the tribes from Forsaken aren't as developed as because they don't have as much material per Tribe than say.... each of the apocalypse tribes getting their own books dedicated to themselves. <br /> <br /> Also the fact that that each is designed to be modular and adaptive to the Storytellers needs .<br /> <br /> <br /> Still, there's enough material worth expanding and defining especially since as of 2e, lots of old content is no longer supported by existing fluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:41:26-07:00","id":864444,"title":"","content":"The major thing I'm shocked at is people coming in here saying there's not enough material to warrant a book for them alone...when the point of a book dedicated to them would be to provide more material.<br /> <br /> It boggles my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:48:20-07:00","id":864449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=864444#post864444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The major thing I'm shocked at is people coming in here saying there's not enough material to warrant a book for them alone...when the point of a book dedicated to them would be to provide more material.<br /> <br /> It boggles my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>They likely mean on a subject as merely concerned with the Tribe itself rather than all the other subjects paired within the suggested books.<br /> <br /> 2e allows for those subjects to be dealt in that fashion because a tribe is basically what it hunts now, beyond their tribal oath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:53:34-07:00","id":864458,"title":"","content":"Weird, a Tribe is a cultural identity based on groups dedicating themselves to a Cosmic Entity and its ideals with a Tribal Oath and Sacred Prey with book ideas detailed in the first post of the thread...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T12:59:59-07:00","id":864465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=864458#post864458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird, a Tribe is a cultural identity based on groups dedicating themselves to a Cosmic Entity and its ideals with a Tribal Oath and Sacred Prey with book ideas detailed in the first post of the thread...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's the thing, they're <i>not</i> a cultural identity, or at least they come with very few cultural identifiers. Adding too many of those risks turning the Tribes into stereotypes. Blood Talons aren't a warrior culture, they seek <i>Glory</i>. Hunters in Darkness don't all lay land mines down in their territories and keep track of where they are, they devote themselves to <i>Cunning</i>. The shared culture of the Tribes ends with the Tribal Oath, Sacred Prey, and Tribal Totem: all of which are going to be skewed by the human cultures that the members grew up in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T13:05:22-07:00","id":864473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=864361#post864361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a lot of good here. I just don't know if the tribes are so developed to warrant a whole book to them like the tribes from apocalypse... But then there's always new material to be written!</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bThere's a reason each of the pitched books is 'One particular tribe *and* their prey/topics related to them/how to handle games relating to that sort of approach/new Gifts, rites and other mechanical widgets'. As I envisage it, for example, the Bone Shadow book would *also* be the 2e Shadow book, etc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T13:09:31-07:00","id":864475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=864473#post864473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThere's a reason each of the pitched books is 'One particular tribe *and* their prey/topics related to them/how to handle games relating to that sort of approach/new Gifts, rites and other mechanical widgets'. As I envisage it, for example, the Bone Shadow book would *also* be the 2e Shadow book, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, that's cool. That'd be the way I'd handle it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T13:14:40-07:00","id":864480,"title":"","content":"Well it's all right there under the spoiler tag in the OP, with a paragraph of rough notions as to what would be in each one <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T13:19:38-07:00","id":864483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=864465#post864465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that's the thing, they're <i>not</i> a cultural identity, or at least they come with very few cultural identifiers. Adding too many of those risks turning the Tribes into stereotypes. Blood Talons aren't a warrior culture, they seek <i>Glory</i>. Hunters in Darkness don't all lay land mines down in their territories and keep track of where they are, they devote themselves to <i><b>PURITY</b></i>. The shared culture of the Tribes ends with the Tribal Oath, Sacred Prey, and Tribal Totem: all of which are going to be skewed by the human cultures that the members grew up in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iron Masters are Cunning, fyi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T13:44:17-07:00","id":864498,"title":"","content":"It appears you're not viewing the cultural identifiers the same way I am, but the point is largely moot since what I mean is right there in the first post of the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T14:06:13-07:00","id":864514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=864483#post864483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Iron Masters are Cunning, fyi.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah snap that's what I get for not playing Werewolf recently enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=864498#post864498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It appears you're not viewing the cultural identifiers the same way I am,</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not, no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monghani:n864498</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">but the point is largely moot since what I mean is right there in the first post of the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's what I get for not rereading the OP when I hop into the thread. Apologies if I came across as defensive or offensive earlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T14:24:48-07:00","id":864530,"title":"","content":"Its cool, just having a foggy mind this week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T15:19:23-07:00","id":864566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=864473#post864473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> \u200bThere's a reason each of the pitched books is 'One particular tribe *and* their prey/topics related to them/how to handle games relating to that sort of approach/new Gifts, rites and other mechanical widgets'. As I envisage it, for example, the Bone Shadow book would *also* be the 2e Shadow book, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>A topic I would greatly appreciate seeing covered is advice and suggestions on how to present and utilize Tribes in your stories. I have to admit, approaching Tribes in how they factor into Packs and Lodges is something I don't quite grasp well. <br /> <br /> How does knowledge spread in a Tribe across members? How do Tribes recruit? What kind of problems are relevant to the different Tribes? What do Tribes offer to its members? Do the Firstborn interact with their Tribes? What's the difference between a multi-Tribe pack and a single Tribe pack? <br /> <br /> These are all questions I wrestle with and I don't have good answers for them. Seeing a book or books delve into these would be greatly helpful to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T15:52:10-07:00","id":864592,"title":"","content":"Hey, since I'm a freelancer now, add me to that list of people interested in writing for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T17:34:18-07:00","id":865215,"title":"","content":"I seem to be a little late for this discussion. Just let me see if a get this right:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Kinslayers</b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Blood Talons Tribe coverage; full new coverage for the Pure and their updated 2e mechanics; heretic and schismatic werewolf groups (weird wolf-cults, strange subgroups of Uratha who follow different ideologies, etc) for Blood Talons and Forsaken in general to clash and interact with; extensive rules for challenges and conflict between Uratha whether for dominance, battle or other things, from the individual level to packs clashing with each other all the way up to Protectorate-scale conflicts; an examination of the pure 'fluff' side of Uratha vs Uratha violence, the taboos, the implications, the different ways various regional Uratha go about these things and their traditions; new fighting styles, Gifts, Rites etc around clashing between Uratha.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Aside from expanding on the Blood Talon tribe, it would probably deal with Ghost Wolves, the Pure, and Bale Hounds. I hope to see playable Pure rules as well as a less black and white scenario among Urdaga and Anshega. As for Bale Hounds, they are my favorites, which would sell me the book just for them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Shadow Hunters</b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Bone Shadow Tribe coverage; definitive coverage of the Shadow, including Deep Shadow, all sorts of phenomena and weirdness, piles of hooks and descriptions of varied Shadow manifestations, more information about Resonance and the interplay between Flesh and Shadow, basically all the creative and mechanical support a GM needs to run the Shadow side of the game; a much deeper look at spirit organisation and politics than ever before to turn spirits into key characters and influences in a game; Totems, dedicating more wordcount to both the ideas and inspiration side of things, but also heftily expanding their mechanical side and offering a new framework to help cover the ascent and growth in power of a totem alongside its pack, the ways the totem and pack affect each other on even a subconscious level, etc; an examination of hunting spirits for the Uratha, with tools, tricks and traps that the Uratha can use against spirits and vice versa; and a section on some Big Names in the Shadow, going into more detail on some Lesser Incarnae, the Firstborn Totems etc, to help GMs with bringing such beings into the game rather than leaving them as distant entities that are never really interacted with.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Aside from expanding on the Bone Shadow tribe, it would give in deep information about Twilight, the Gauntlet, and the Shadow: Ghosts, Ectoplasm, Hisil Landscape, Spirits and even weirder things. Might overlap a little with Kinslayers as it should cover the Maeljin and Wounds.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Sacred Ground</b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Hunter in Darkness Tribe coverage; new rules for territory and the surrounding issues, such as shaping your territory, making territory a key element in clashing with other Uratha, more info on Loci, the role prey take in the territory, etc; more information on the Gauntlet itself, exploring how to bring it into a game not just as a basic boundary but as a place with strange phenomena, discussion of what lies *within* it, etc; full new coverage of the Hosts, with more detailed rules than are present in the corebook and a better examination of Host society, their goals and how they go about them, including coverage for what happens when the Hosts are successful and begin to regain the divine power of their progenitors; coverage of how Uratha interact with certain other peripheral realms (possibly including the Hedge and Underworld); and maybe new Hunting Ground write-ups or examples of specific Sacred Places that the Uratha and Hunters in Darkness hold as sacred ground.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Aside from expanding on the Hunter in Darkness tribe, it would be our new Territories with the added subject of Hosts: Patrolling, territory mechanics like Damnation City, in deep Host rules and even new hosts. This also might cover Pagaeans, since Rat and Spider were those, and even give us new legends to seed our stories.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Watchdogs</b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Iron Master Tribe coverage; more rules for humanity as prey, including specific prey-groups from cultists to corporations and how they can both be a threat to and be threatened by the Uratha; rules for human shamen expanded out of the Rites system; an examination of the difficulties of maintaining a human cover amidst society for an Uratha, the challenges of hunting in dense urban areas and amongst human communities in general, and how humans drastically shape the spiritual reflection of the world; changes in technology and science, and both the challenges Uratha can face from these, the challenges they faced in previous technological eras, and the ways technology and change contribute to the benefit of the Uratha and the Iron Masters; and coverage of Uratha trying to affect the human population on a much largerscale, like trying to shape the destiny of nations or enslave entire regions to the machinations of spirit-gods or whatnot.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Aside from expanding on the Iron Master tribe, it would give us information on how technology affects the Uratha, and how mortals become capable of harnessing the power of the Hisil and use it against the wolves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Heirs to the Hunt</b></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Storm Lord Tribe coverage; deeper coverage of Claimed with more mechanics, as well as new types of Claimed horror; an examination of other weird elements of possessions and otherworldy invaders, including new antagonist types; Forsaken politics, including on a wide scale, including traditions and cultures around thereof, how Tribes and packs and Lodges interact to affect the balance of power; more extensive coverage around Protectorates, including how and why they form, system support for Protectorates and their effects, etc; and wordcount and more mechanical support for high Primal Urge werewolves, the paths available for them to take, how they affect the world and how they, in turn, are changed.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Aside from expanding on the Storm Lord tribe, it would give us deeper Claiming and Politics rules. It will clearly overlap with Watchdogs and Sacred Ground, but done right this might add a lot of info on those topics. I'm really curious about &quot;new antagonists&quot;, I guess Spirits will receive a lot of new ways to transform flesh into monstrosity. I advise covering the Indigam here, since they are the threats that unite Forsaken, and thus generate the most &quot;politiking&quot; you will ever find in a chronicle of Uratha.<br /> <br /> <br /> Count me in, boys. If I got this right, I would buy every single one of those books, twice if needed for them to become reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5446,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","user":"BinAly","date":". 04-13-2016, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T19:07:57-07:00","id":865266,"title":"","content":"The downside to doing the books this way (tribe + prey) is that it's great if you love Blood Talons, poor if you like Storm Lords. If (and that's a definite *if*) Rich went for this, with pre-planning, writing, development, and production, you'd be looking at *maybe* the first book by end 2016/early 2017, and if the production line speeds up, Storm Lords by 2019/2020.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd rather have the 5 tribes in one book, and prey in another, and hopefully have both by mid next year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T19:19:31-07:00","id":865268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=865266#post865266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The downside to doing the books this way (tribe + prey) is that it's great if you love Blood Talons, poor if you like Storm Lords. If (and that's a definite *if*) Rich went for this, with pre-planning, writing, development, and production, you'd be looking at *maybe* the first book by end 2016/early 2017, and if the production line speeds up, Storm Lords by 2019/2020.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd rather have the 5 tribes in one book, and prey in another, and hopefully have both by mid next year.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is, I don't see much to cover just for the Tribes. It will end up being a new gifts and rites list if you con't include extensive info about their sacred prey, and that is a lot of words for just one book. In the end, even if we get a single Tribes book, their prey will only be covered by the end of the same time-line you pointed. Unless they are able to compile all the preys into a &quot;Book of Prey&quot;, which might not do justice to the sheer amount of story seeds and mechanics all the preys should deliver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T19:20:07-07:00","id":865270,"title":"","content":"This is true, but that opens up some interesting questions about how digital distribution can be played around with.<br /> <br /> More questions I currently want to tackle, but you know, it's a new era, we can think about products in different ways.<br /> <br /> Though the inevitability of print does kick that in somewhat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T19:20:26-07:00","id":865271,"title":"","content":"Predators had spirits, a little bit on hosts, and ridden and claimed in it, but it didn't go much into the Hisil. I couldn't see a book like that tackling the Pure and Bale Hounds and humanity as a threat too, at least not while also doing them all justice. And as good as Tribes of the Moon was, it was still pretty limited.<br /> <br /> It doesn't look like third edition is coming anytime soon, so we do seem to have time for five rather than two books. While it would be nice if things were faster, it's hard to tell for customers and fans lately how much of that is due to the Paradox buyout throughout the past year, that Rich Thomas said slowed down production. Recently we've actually had a pretty big surge of releases, so perhaps things are speeding up at the tail end.<br /> <br /> If Paradox starts publishing old World of Darkness stuff, too, there may be less work to do on those lines.<br /> <br /> But yes, whoever likes the last tribe gets the shaft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-13-2016, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T19:26:09-07:00","id":865273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=865271#post865271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yes, whoever likes the last tribe gets the shaft.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they get the shaft by a lot, though. Every prey is a prey for all Tribes, just no their specialty. Storm Lords also battle other Uratha, Hosts and humans, which are covered by the first books. The order seems pretty nice, with Werewolf antagonists and interactions being covered first (which also cover how the Moon Tribes interact), and the Hisil getting the second place (which is everything you need to run a true Uratha chronicle, and no book in 2E really delivers Shadow information). All in all, I think it is a good way to build a strong gameline that has all its ends covered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T19:42:44-07:00","id":865278,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion\">Putting this up here</a>, since we can expect any Werewolf supplement to (likely) feature new Gifts.<br /> <br /> Plus, until we have more material out on the Pure, I'm going with my own conversions for the Pure Gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T20:13:57-07:00","id":865292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=865268#post865268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem is, I don't see much to cover just for the Tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I don't agree with this, the model I'd prefer to see would be:<br /> <br /> Children of the Wolf - Covers the Forsaken tribes, the Pure, the Bale Hounds, and expands on possibilities of hidden or lost tribes, new tribes coming up, and how the possible transition of large lodge to small tribe might work.<br /> <br /> What Lurks in Shadow - Covers most of the prey except humans, and werewolves. Spirits, the <i>Hisil</i>, ridden, claimed, the hosts, how the <i>idigam</i> have upset the apple cart. More detail on playing in the Shadow, and hunting that part of the pack's territory.<br /> <br /> Heirs of Man - Humans, Wolf-Blooded, living in the modern world filled with internet, wireless surveillance, near ubiquitous recording devices, and human coordination. Explores the shifting nature of the Hunt, how it is both timeless and adaptable. Modern times give more agency to WB and humans than every before. Examine how these peripherals view the werewolves, and the nature of the pack specifically from the outsiders point of view. Introduce more options for focusing play on the periphery. Not Uratha-less packs. More what changes when your entire game is low-to-zero-powered people inhabiting a frightening world of violence and horror driven by madness-inducing demigods at the hub?<br /> <br /> Then expand whatever else needs expanding. There's always something. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T21:36:15-07:00","id":865320,"title":"","content":"I think your &quot;Children of Wolf&quot; book crams in way too much. You can do all 5 Forsaken Tribes in one book fairly plausibly, but you're not going to have room for strong Pure and Bale Houund, Lost Tribes, etc coverage in the same volume.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T21:59:20-07:00","id":865325,"title":"","content":"I'd honestly like to see a book on the Tribes (stuffed with snapshots of history, new Gifts, possibly a handful of Lodges, and rumors of lost Tribes or Tribes to come), a book of antagonists (give the Pure a pretty hefty chapter, then toss some wordcount at mortals, Bale Hounds, skinchangers, and the like), and then another book that devotes itself fully to Spirits and the Shadow (both describing possibly enemies and allies/totems/packmates, and what the Shadow is like when you roam it and partially live in it). I'd also love to see the Werewolf equivalent of Equinox Road, covering what happens at Primal Urge 7-10, extensive material on Idigam, and then some possible truths about Father Wolf, Luna, and the Firstborn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T22:05:19-07:00","id":865327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=865325#post865325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd honestly like to see a book on the Tribes (stuffed with snapshots of history, new Gifts, possibly a handful of Lodges, and rumors of lost Tribes or Tribes to come), a book of antagonists (give the Pure a pretty hefty chapter, then toss some wordcount at mortals, Bale Hounds, skinchangers, and the like), and then another book that devotes itself fully to Spirits and the Shadow (both describing possibly enemies and allies/totems/packmates, and what the Shadow is like when you roam it and partially live in it). I'd also love to see the Werewolf equivalent of Equinox Road, covering what happens at Primal Urge 7-10, extensive material on Idigam, and then some possible truths about Father Wolf, Luna, and the Firstborn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You might check out Tribes of the Moon, the Pure, Blasphemies and Predators, which is basically what you're describing, beyond the 'end game' stuff.<br /> <br /> The problem with a book on all the tribes is that it doesn't get the room to really flesh them out very well. As evidence I'd point to Tribes of the Moon. And the Bale Hounds already had some wordcount 'tossed' at them long ago and it's left fans wanting more, while a book devoted entirely to the Shadow is probably going to be a blue book, since it's something that multiple game lines are going to be involved in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-14-2016, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T22:06:18-07:00","id":865328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=865327#post865327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You might check out Tribes of the Moon, the Pure, Blasphemies and Predators, which is basically what you're describing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah, but with the benefit of a greater understanding of the line and 2e rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T02:26:13-07:00","id":865375,"title":"","content":"I still thinks that proper Bale Hounds should be part of 2E I<b>nferno</b> book as one of it's chapter ( other would be Belial Brood, rest to the Inferno directly ) - those groups are always &quot;wicked stepchildren&quot; of proper gamelines, but one chapter on specifics of Bale Hounds will be enough if rest of book will talk about Malejins as part of Inferno realm. Not that some thoughts should not be shown in <b>Kinslayers</b>, but core of it should be in new <b>Inferno</b> book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T02:49:30-07:00","id":865382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=865375#post865375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still thinks that proper Bale Hounds should be part of 2E I<b>nferno</b> book as one of it's chapter ( other would be Belial Brood, rest to the Inferno directly ) - those groups are always &quot;wicked stepchildren&quot; of proper gamelines, but one chapter on specifics of Bale Hounds will be enough if rest of book will talk about Malejins as part of Inferno realm. Not that some thoughts should not be shown in <b>Kinslayers</b>, but core of it should be in new <b>Inferno</b> book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I definitely don't think Belial's Brood should be in the inferno book, given they're not a group with any ties to the inferno at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T03:08:33-07:00","id":865387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=865375#post865375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still thinks that proper Bale Hounds should be part of 2E I<b>nferno</b> book as one of it's chapter ( other would be Belial Brood, rest to the Inferno directly ) - those groups are always &quot;wicked stepchildren&quot; of proper gamelines, but one chapter on specifics of Bale Hounds will be enough if rest of book will talk about Malejins as part of Inferno realm. Not that some thoughts should not be shown in <b>Kinslayers</b>, but core of it should be in new <b>Inferno</b> book.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a waste of significant word count for quite a lot of groups who don't play werewolf and couldn't care less about Bale Hounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T03:31:41-07:00","id":865390,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd rather Bale Hounds be in a Werewolf product than a blue book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=865266#post865266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The downside to doing the books this way (tribe + prey) is that it's great if you love Blood Talons, poor if you like Storm Lords. If (and that's a definite *if*) Rich went for this, with pre-planning, writing, development, and production, you'd be looking at *maybe* the first book by end 2016/early 2017, and if the production line speeds up, Storm Lords by 2019/2020.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd rather have the 5 tribes in one book, and prey in another, and hopefully have both by mid next year.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure. Thing is, something's *always* gonna get the short end of the stick, time-wise. The list of five I had was in the order it was because alphabetical Tribes, not as a necessary demand for publication in that order - and I am fully aware that it may not mesh with what Stew has in mind for forthcoming books regardless - but I don't see it as innately worse than 'book on tribes, book on werewolf prey, book on other prey, book on shadow, book on territories, book on humans' etc.<br /> <br /> I don't think Requiem or Awakening particularly suffered due to having a series of Covenant/Order books where, indeed, some had to wait longer than others.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T03:54:43-07:00","id":865398,"title":"","content":"The bale hounds do deserve at least some mention in an Inferno 2e book, at least describing them from the perspective of inferno related beings. Definitely not a full chapter though. A set of rules for making them as npcs without requiring the WtF book would be a good idea for it. Like what we got with the demon stg, but either using the rules contained within the Inferno book or the horror system from the core. This is getting a bit off topic though, so I'm gonna stop talking Inferno here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T04:48:22-07:00","id":865421,"title":"","content":"Bale Hounds being in an Inferno book really depend if they're going to be linked to the Inferno at all, which isn't a guarantee in second edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T04:52:21-07:00","id":865423,"title":"","content":"True, I do like wounds, wound spirits and bale hounds being the inferno tainting the hisil though and for now it's easiest to assume they are, given that's how it was in first edition, at least until Stew or one of the writers confirms otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T06:09:43-07:00","id":865452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425614-petition-for-tribes-of-the-moon-2e-working-title?p=865390#post865390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'd rather Bale Hounds be in a Werewolf product than a blue book.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sure. Thing is, something's *always* gonna get the short end of the stick, time-wise. The list of five I had was in the order it was because alphabetical Tribes, not as a necessary demand for publication in that order - and I am fully aware that it may not mesh with what Stew has in mind for forthcoming books regardless - but I don't see it as innately worse than 'book on tribes, book on werewolf prey, book on other prey, book on shadow, book on territories, book on humans' etc.<br /> <br /> I don't think Requiem or Awakening particularly suffered due to having a series of Covenant/Order books where, indeed, some had to wait longer than others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. I don't view any one approach as the one true way, and none of them would stop me jumping to write for them anyway <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T12:28:09-07:00","id":973291,"title":"","content":"And now we see that the Tribal Pillars and various Lodges(with their Secrets and Blasphemies not removed like they were in The Pack) would make for an excellent chapter for each Tribebook as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T13:32:40-07:00","id":973353,"title":"","content":"Sign me up, i would throw cash so fast for a new werewolf book or books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:25:58-07:00","id":973805,"title":"","content":"After neglecting this thread for far too long, I've updated the list of supporters and suggestions for the new books. From what I understand, pitch season is at the end of every year, so now's a good time to give this thr